From ff37860ef4d3e2cfbb5f8277cae0febec1fd0589 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] style-manager: Glass look of the password prompt at startup

The keyboard takes the look of unl0kr's theme plinius-glass, the password
prompt at startup (buffybox in pkgbuilds/buffybox):

- New stylesheet plinius-glass.css after common.css: white glass keys,
  darker glass for system keys, toggles and return, thin translucent
  borders, the accent color while pressed, regular weight, popups in the
  colors of the prompt's dropdown list
- Keys get 1px instead of 2px margin beside each other (rows unchanged),
  so the character and number keys become wider
- The wallpaper Phosh shows (dark variant with a dark color scheme,
  first picture of a slideshow) is rendered small and blurred in a
  thread: the bottom part the keyboard covers, as PNG under
  $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/stevia; it becomes the darkened background of
  pos-input-surface. Without a wallpaper or with high contrast the
  plain dark color stays.
- A custom accent color from org.plinius.appearance (phosh-plinius)
  wins over GNOME's accent enum
- The accent provider was stored in css_provider, so every change of the
  accent color stacked one more provider; it goes to accent_css_provider
---
